Quality Scenarios

QS1 — Search Performance:
Source: University community member
Stimulus: User searches for a club
Environment: Normal operating conditions
Artifact: Club search functionality
Response: System retrieves and displays matching clubs
Measure: Search results shall be displayed within 3 seconds of submitting a search.

QS2 — System Availability:
Source: University community member
Stimulus: User attempts to access the platform
Environment: Normal university operating hours
Artifact: University Clubs Hub
Response: System allows the user to access the platform
Measure: The platform shall maintain at least 99% availability during normal operating periods.

QS3 — Usability:
Source: First-time user
Stimulus: User wants to find a club
Environment: User has no previous experience with the platform
Artifact: Search and navigation interface
Response: User searches for and views a relevant club
Measure: At least 90% of first-time users shall be able to find and open a relevant club within 2 minutes without assistance during usability testing.

QS4 — Security:
Source: Unauthorized user
Stimulus: Attempts to modify club information or submit a venue request
Environment: Normal system operation
Artifact: Club management and venue-request functions
Response: System rejects the unauthorized action
Measure: 100% of unauthorized modification attempts shall be rejected.

QS5 — Reliability:
Source: Administrative staff member
Stimulus: Approves or rejects a venue request
Environment: Normal system operation
Artifact: Venue booking record
Response: System stores and displays the updated booking status
Measure: 100% of successfully submitted booking decisions shall be persisted correctly
